  "published": "2026-08-26T01:31:38.1Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TCMProject.Web: sets JWT ClockSkew to 60s (was TimeSpan.Zero) in AddAuthenticationService. With the access token now 1h (down from 30 days), the exp/nbf boundary is crossed hourly instead of monthly; with zero skew, a few seconds of clock drift between the identity server and a validating service would reject a freshly issued token as \"not yet valid\" with sporadic 401s. 60s absorbs typical NTP drift at no real security cost (the token is already short) and aligns with the 60s buffer of the frontend silent refresh. Additive; no API change.",
